.Dd September 19, 2026
.Dt SHUTDOWN 2
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm shutdown
.Nd shut down a connected stream socket
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.In sys/socket.h
.Ft int
.Fn shutdown "int fd" "int how"
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Fn shutdown
operates on the connected TCP socket
.Fa fd .
A listener, an unconnected socket, and a datagram socket cannot be
shut down.
A stream has a connection for this purpose after its handshake has
completed and while its connection record remains attached in a
subsequent closing state.
.Pp
The
.Fa how
argument selects a direction:
.Bl -tag -width SHUT_RDWR
.It Dv SHUT_RD
Value 0.
Accepted without effect.
Input remains available.
.It Dv SHUT_WR
Value 1.
Start the normal TCP close and detach the connection record from the
socket.
In the established or close-wait state, queued output is sent before
the FIN, so the peer receives end of input after those bytes.
In other connected closing states, the connection record is freed.
.It Dv SHUT_RDWR
Value 2.
The same operation as
.Dv SHUT_WR .
.El
.Pp
Unlike Linux, a write-side shutdown does not preserve the connection
for continued receiving.
It uses the same TCP close operation as the final close of the socket.
The descriptor remains open, but a later
.Fn shutdown
fails with
.Er ENOTCONN .
.Pp
This operation is subcall 13 of i386
.Xr socketcall 2 ,
system call 102.
.Sh RETURN VALUES
.Fn shutdown
returns zero on success.
On failure it returns -1 and sets
.Va errno .
The kernel interface returns the negative error number.
.Sh EXAMPLES
The default suite's
.Pa tests/loopprobe.c
shuts a connected client down with
.Dv SHUT_WR ,
checks that a send then fails with
.Er EPIPE ,
and checks that a blocking and a nonblocking read return zero.
.Sh ERRORS
.Bl -tag -width "[EOPNOTSUPP]"
.It Bq Er EBADF
.Fa fd
is not an open descriptor.
.It Bq Er EFAULT
The
.Fn socketcall
argument array cannot be read.
.It Bq Er EINVAL
.Fa how
is not 0, 1, or 2.
.It Bq Er ENOTCONN
The socket is not a connected stream, including a listener, a
datagram socket, an incomplete handshake, or a socket whose
connection record has been detached.
.It Bq Er ENOTSOCK
.Fa fd
does not refer to a socket.
.It Bq Er EOPNOTSUPP
The socket is a raw socket.
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr connect 2 ,
.Xr recv 2 ,
.Xr send 2 ,
.Xr socket 2 ,
.Xr socketcall 2
